{{Quote|Won't the big boss be angry that you didn't wait for his approval to attack the Mourner's Wail, ''General Vukorah''?''"<br />"''He won't notice. Hasn't left his tower in years, grieving all this time.|An Unbroken Clan [[soldier]] and Vukorah|<ref name="Bounty Hunters 3">[[Bounty Hunters 3|''Bounty Hunters'' 3]]</ref>}}
The '''Unbroken Clan Palace''',<ref name="Bounty Hunters 20" /> also known as the '''Unbroken Clan Fortress''',<ref name="BH 33">[[Bounty Hunters 33|''Bounty Hunters'' 33]]</ref> or the '''Unbroken Clan Sanctuary''',<ref name="BH 34">[[Bounty Hunters 34|''Bounty Hunters'' 34]]</ref> was a [[fortress]] located on the<ref name="Bounty Hunters 20" /> [[planet]]<ref name="Databank">{{Databank|corellia|Corellia}}</ref> [[Corellia]] that was owned by the [[Krynthia's father|Grand Leader]] of the [[Unbroken Clan]] criminal syndicate. After the [[Mission to Corellia (Nakano Lash's crew)|death]] of his daughter,<ref name="Bounty Hunters 20" /> [[Krynthia]],<ref name="Bounty Hunters 4">[[Bounty Hunters 4|''Bounty Hunters'' 4]]</ref> the [[Grand Leader]] locked himself in the palace for [[Standard year|years]] and mourned her [[death]].<ref name="Bounty Hunters 20" /> Between [[3 ABY]] and [[4 ABY]],<ref name="Date note">The events of [[Bounty Hunters 20|''Bounty Hunters'' 20]] take place after the [[Escape from Cloud City]] and before the [[Rescue of Han Solo]], which are dated to [[3 ABY]] and [[4 ABY]], respectively, by ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''. Therefore, the events of ''Bounty Hunters'' 20 must take place between those two [[Standard year|years]].</ref> the syndicate's [[General]] [[Vukorah]] traveled to the palace where she [[Assassination of the Unbroken Clan Grand Leader|killed]] the Grand Leader, and took over the Unbroken Clan.<ref name="Bounty Hunters 20" />

